  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Complete exterior interpretation of the mapped smithy/carpentry range at Yasnaya Polyana: gray log workshop on a low red-brick plinth, broad weathered-board hip roof, single red-brick chimney, recessed warm wooden double door beneath a shallow supported hood, and a genuinely open timber-post lean-to alongside the room. Original map outline anchors the complete envelope; the long rear extent is map-led and hidden in the front photographs. All canopy and hood supports remain present in every LOD. No invented forge interior, machinery, merchandise, copied signs, inscriptions, artwork, people or photograph pixels. Hidden rear doors/windows and exact historical roof/support inventory remain approximate. Approximate photo-led scale: log eaves2.55m, board hip rise2.2m and one capped brick chimney to5.38m above floor. Double doorway2.12m; shallow hood at2.25..2.45m and adjacent lean-to2.2..2.45m. Hidden rear range, canopy depth, post inventory, roof condition, thresholds and accessibility approximate; no exact mapped height is supplied. Retained Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen201x201/6m ground; outside northeast approach provider[2.3,10] supplies205.2228043360681m datum. Whole boundary grades-1.487..0.038m, floor+0.2m and closed room foundation/support bottoms-1.7m. Original ground remains under the open side canopy; occupied room,11 post feet and two entry aprons alone cut it. Coarse downhill plinth/support exposure can reach about1.7m, higher than the visible front-photo plinth; hidden levels remain approximate. No flattening or bespoke terrain. Independent neighbors, approach, roads and ponds remain. Front pictures establish the log room, hip/chimney, double door/hood and left open canopy; trees/fence and perspective conceal rear depth. The mapped14.3m extent is therefore an explicit reconstruction of hidden room/canopy depth, not an exact inventory from a rear photo. Absolute front assignment follows the photographed approach/valley and the retained road wrapping northwest/southwest, not merely the closest road. Hidden doors/windows, roof/post inventory, thresholds and accessibility remain approximate. Fixed synthetic planes partly bury grade-specific plinth/aprons; whole/native views cover the envelope. Other estate structures remain procedural context in this isolated fixture. Physical phone/laptop and dense-city timings remain pending."
  },
